Day 54/100 of #DrGVishwanathanChallenge
Today, I solved two Binary Tree problems in Java
-Problem 1: 2236. (Root Equals Sum of Children)

-Approach:
 This problem was straightforward. I simply checked whether the value of the root node is equal to the sum of its left and right child.

Time Complexity: O(1)
 Space Complexity: O(1)

-Problem 2: 226. (Invert Binary Tree)

-Approach:
 For every node, I recursively inverted its left and right subtrees and then swapped them. The key idea was to visit each node and reverse its children.

Time Complexity: O(n)
 Space Complexity: O(h) due to the recursion stack, where h is the height of the tree.
